## Documentation

Docs follow Diátaxis under `docs/`. All four quadrants are first-class: never
skip one because it seems unneeded. A doc that mixes quadrants gets split.

- `docs/tutorial/`: learning-oriented walkthroughs. Start with `getting-started.md`.
- `docs/how-to/`: task-oriented recipes. `verify-a-change.md`: how to check a step and report it. Read before stating how a step will be verified and before reporting the result.
- `docs/reference/`: lookups. `repo-conventions.md`: commit messages, code comments and prose that lands in the repo.
- `docs/explanation/`: design rationale. `harness.md`: why the guardrails exist.

<!-- Add one line per doc, in the form "Read before changing X". -->

Update the relevant documentation in the same commit when the documented
behavior changes.

## Workflow

Work is split into small steps, one commit each.

Before implementing a step:
1. State the intended behavior.
2. State the relevant constraints or rules.
3. List the files that change and, per file, what changes in one line.
4. State how the result will be verified (`docs/how-to/verify-a-change.md`).
5. Wait for approval before making changes.

After implementing, run the checks and report the results as
`docs/how-to/verify-a-change.md` describes.

Before every commit, run `/harness:prepare-commit`. For a plan, use
`/harness:plan-slices`.

